#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:249
msgid "Building Catalog Blueprints"
msgstr "Building Catalog Blueprints"

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:253
msgid ""
"|morpheus| Blueprints allow for full multi-tier application deployment. "
"In the Self Service catalog, user can create catalog items based on pre-"
"existing App Blueprints. If new Blueprints need to be created for the "
"Service Catalog, see other sections of |morpheus| docs on building App "
"Blueprints of various supported types. Just like with catalog Instances, "
"we can pre-configure Blueprints and present them to users viewing the "
"Service Catalog Persona view for easy, one-click deployment."
msgstr "|morpheus| Blueprints allow for full multi-tier application deployment. In the Self Service catalog, user can create catalog items based on pre-existing App Blueprints. If new Blueprints need to be created for the Service Catalog, see other sections of |morpheus| docs on building App Blueprints of various supported types. Just like with catalog Instances, we can pre-configure Blueprints and present them to users viewing the Service Catalog Persona view for easy, one-click deployment."

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:255
msgid ""
"From the Catalog Items List Page (|LibBluCat|), click :guilabel:`ADD`. "
"From the dropdown menu, select Blueprint. The modal window will appear to"
" configure and add a new catalog Blueprint."
msgstr "From the Catalog Items List Page (|LibBluCat|), click :guilabel:`ADD`. From the dropdown menu, select Blueprint. The modal window will appear to configure and add a new catalog Blueprint."

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:272
msgid ""
"**CONFIGURE:** Click :guilabel:`CONFIGURE` to use the familiar App "
"provisioning wizard to tie Blueprint and App deployment configuration to "
"the Catalog Item"
msgstr "**CONFIGURE:** Click :guilabel:`CONFIGURE` to use the familiar App provisioning wizard to tie Blueprint and App deployment configuration to the Catalog Item"

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:273
msgid ""
"**APP SPEC:** Inject App spec here for any fields required to provision "
"an App from your Blueprint. You may also inject any overrides to the "
"existing Blueprint spec that are desired. App Spec configuration must be "
"YAML, a simple example that names the App and sets the Group and Cloud is"
" included below:"
msgstr "**APP SPEC:** Inject App spec here for any fields required to provision an App from your Blueprint. You may also inject any overrides to the existing Blueprint spec that are desired. App Spec configuration must be YAML, a simple example that names the App and sets the Group and Cloud is included below:"

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:275
msgid ""
"#Example App Spec\n"
"\n"
"name: '<%= customOption.appName %>'\n"
"group:\n"
"  name: Dev Group\n"
"environment: Dev\n"
"tiers:\n"
"  Web:\n"
"    instances:\n"
"      - instance:\n"
"          type: nginx\n"
"          cloud: Dev AWS\n"
"  App:\n"
"    instances:\n"
"      - instance:\n"
"          type: apache\n"
"          cloud: Dev AWS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:295
#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:331
msgid ""
"**CONTENT:** Optionally include documentation content for this Catalog "
"Item. Markdown-formatted text is accepted and displayed appropriately "
"when the item is ordered from the Service Catalog. A new Catalog Item-"
"type Wiki entry will also be added containing this information."
msgstr "**CONTENT:** Optionally include documentation content for this Catalog Item. Markdown-formatted text is accepted and displayed appropriately when the item is ordered from the Service Catalog. A new Catalog Item-type Wiki entry will also be added containing this information."

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:297
msgid ""
"App spec custom option variables should be single quoted in YAML: "
"``cloud: '<%= customOption.cloud %>'``. Additionally, not all variables "
"are available here as many are unknown until provisioning. Users may use "
"any custom Input values (customOption) as well as name or hostname values"
" which are resolved as part of naming policy evaluation."
msgstr "App spec custom option variables should be single quoted in YAML: ``cloud: '<%= customOption.cloud %>'``. Additionally, not all variables are available here as many are unknown until provisioning. Users may use any custom Input values (customOption) as well as name or hostname values which are resolved as part of naming policy evaluation."

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:303
#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:336
msgid "Tip"
msgstr "Conseil"

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:303
#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:336
msgid ""
"There are a number of advantages to using Forms over Inputs. See the "
"section above on using Forms with Catalog Items for a complete "
"description on how they are used and the advantages to using them."
msgstr "There are a number of advantages to using Forms over Inputs. See the section above on using Forms with Catalog Items for a complete description on how they are used and the advantages to using them."

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:309
msgid "Building Catalog Workflows"
msgstr "Building Catalog Workflows"

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:313
msgid ""
"From the Catalog Items List Page (|LibBluCat|), click :guilabel:`ADD`. "
"From the dropdown menu, select Workflow. The modal window will appear to "
"configure and add a new catalog Workflow."
msgstr "From the Catalog Items List Page (|LibBluCat|), click :guilabel:`ADD`. From the dropdown menu, select Workflow. The modal window will appear to configure and add a new catalog Workflow."

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:322
msgid ""
"**ENABLED:** When checked, this Workflow item will be available for "
"selection in the Service Catalog"
msgstr "**ENABLED:** When checked, this Workflow item will be available for selection in the Service Catalog"

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:328
msgid ""
"**WORKFLOW:** Select an existing Workflow to be associated with this "
"Catalog Item, new Workflows are created in :menuselection:`Library --> "
"Automation`"
msgstr "**WORKFLOW:** Select un/una existente Flujo de trabajo a be asociado/asociada avec este/esta Catalog Item, nuevo/nueva Workflows sont creado/creada dans |LibAut|"

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:329
msgid ""
"**CONTEXT:** Optionally restrict users to a specific target context, "
"Instance, Server, or None"
msgstr "**CONTEXT:** Restreignez éventuellement les utilisateurs à un contexte cible spécifique : Instance, Server ou None"

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:330
msgid ""
"**CONFIG:** Enter an optional custom config JSON body. See `Workflows "
"documentation "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/library/automation/workflows.html"
"#allow-custom-config>`_ for a formatting example"
msgstr "**CONFIG:** Saisissez un corps JSON de configuration personnalisé optionnel. Consultez `Workflows documentation <https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/library/automation/workflows.html#allow-custom-config>`_ pour un exemple de formatage"

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:341
msgid "Editing and Deleting from the Self Service Catalog"
msgstr "Modification et suppression depuis le catalogue libre-service"

#: ../../library/blueprints/self-service.rst:343
msgid ""
"Once created, Service Catalog items can be edited or deleted from the "
"Catalog Items list view (|LibBluCat|). Click the pencil icon in the "
"relevant row to edit the Service Catalog item or the trash can icon to "
"delete it. Alternatively, Service Catalog items can be made inactive to "
"remove them as provisioning options rather than deleting them."
msgstr "Une fois créés, les éléments du catalogue de services peuvent être modifiés ou supprimés depuis la vue liste des éléments du catalogue (|LibBluCat|). Cliquez sur l'icône crayon dans la ligne correspondante pour modifier l'élément du catalogue de services ou sur l'icône corbeille pour le supprimer. Alternativement, les éléments du catalogue de services peuvent être rendus inactifs pour les retirer des options de provisionnement plutôt que de les supprimer."

#: ../../library/blueprints/clusterLayouts.rst:4
msgid ""
"|morpheus| includes many different types of Cluster Layouts out-of-the-"
